<!--
  CONTROL PROBE - not detection content, and not part of the exercise.

  The PUC2 2c rules now live in ruleset/rules, because nothing analysisd loaded
  ever mentioned them while they sat here. That conclusion rests on an
  assumption: that Wazuh warns when if_sid names a signature that does not
  exist. It does so for the built-in rules 80781 and 80784 on every startup,
  but an assumption about the instrument is exactly what has been wrong before.

  So this file is the negative half of a controlled pair. Rule 100198 lives
  here in etc/rules and rule 100199 lives with the real rules in ruleset/rules.
  Both are built to be rejected loudly and both are ignored once rejected, so
  neither can fire, alert or touch a training level.

    both warn      -> both directories load; the rules were always loaded and
                      the fault is somewhere else entirely
    only 100199    -> etc/rules is not read on this image; the move was right
    neither warns  -> the canary proves nothing and this whole line of
                      reasoning has to be thrown away

  Delete this file and its task once the answer is recorded.
-->
<group name="puc2,control,">

  <rule id="100198" level="0">
    <if_sid>999998</if_sid>
    <description>PUC2 control probe in etc/rules: must be rejected with a warning naming 100198</description>
  </rule>

</group>
